  Energy budget for 30 km range at 389W cruise:
  Travel time: 30km / 50km/h = 0.6 hours
  Energy needed: 389W × 0.6h = 233 Wh
  Battery mass: 233Wh / 250Wh/kg = 0.93 kg (optimistic)
  Practical estimate (70% DoD, 80% drivetrain): ~2.5 kg battery
  
  Hovering overhead: ~100W for active stabilization
  Total system power: 389W propulsion + 100W levitation = 489W
  Adjusted range: 15-20 km (realistic), 30 km (optimized conditions)

KINETIC ENERGY RECOVERY:
  Regenerative braking: P_regen = η_regen × ½mv²
  At 50→0 km/h stop: E = ½×90×13.9² = 8685 J = 2.4 Wh
  Recovery efficiency: ~70% → 1.7 Wh per full stop
  Meaningful over many stops in urban riding

SOLAR POWER SUPPLEMENT:
  Thin-film solar cell: 100-150 W/m²
  Bike top surface: ~0.5 m²
  Power: 50-75W peak
  Daily charge (6h sun): 300-450 Wh
